    "result_text": "The build is green \u2014 all 34 tests pass, including the four that target this change (Cp15, Cp21, Cp23, Cp24).\n\nHere's what I changed to satisfy the specification:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Replaced the `membershipTier` string property with `membershipLevel` (integer, min 1 / max 3, `readOnly`). Since the DTOs are generated from this spec at build time, this removes `membershipTier` from the response and adds `membershipLevel`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Retargeted the mapping to `membershipLevel` and replaced `membershipTier(...)` with a new `membershipLevel(Owner)` method implementing the rules: start at 1, +1 when a non-blank email is present, +1 when `namesakeCount == 0`, capped at 3. The old GOLD/household logic (`householdMemberCount`) is gone, as required \u2014 a 3-member household no longer yields a special tier.\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 Updated the create audit line to record `membershipLevel={}` (derived via the mapper) alongside the id it already logged, instead of recording tier.\n\nThe `membershipLevel` computation runs after `saveOwner`, so `namesakeCount` is already populated when the audit line and DTO are produced. Note that level 4 is deliberately left unreachable (reserved for tenure), and `householdMemberCount` is still computed by the service but is no longer used for the level.",
